From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 13:40:11 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: gcc-glymur: Keep the USB GDSCs in retention

All USB controller and USB PHY GDSCs on Glymur are described with
PWRSTS_OFF_ON, so they are switched off when their consumers suspend.
The DWC3 controllers and the QMP PHYs lose their configuration when that
happens, and their drivers do not reprogram everything on resume. After
system suspend a USB-C controller can fault in the SMMU and stop working.

X1E80100 describes the same ten domains with PWRSTS_RET_ON, which
leaves them on in software and lets the hardware put them in retention
when the parent domain collapses. Do the same on Glymur. The USB4
router GDSCs are unchanged.

Fixes: efe504300a17 ("clk: qcom: gcc: Add support for Global Clock Controller")
Assisted-by: Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-glymur.c | 20 ++++++++++----------
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-glymur.c b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-glymur.c
index 2ee4820b6fd..c96bbad9ac3 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-glymur.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-glymur.c
@@ -7785,7 +7785,7 @@ static struct gdsc gcc_usb20_prim_gdsc = {
 	.pd = {
 		.name = "gcc_usb20_prim_gdsc",
 	},
-	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_OFF_ON,
+	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_RET_ON,
 	.flags = POLL_CFG_GDSCR | RETAIN_FF_ENABLE,
 };
 
